                <pb facs="0247" n="139" xml:id="pg139"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Thompson to Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Rio
                                de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-03-12"><hi rendition="#italic">March 12, 1894</hi></date>.
                        (Received March 12.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Thompson reports that Saldanha da Gama has asked for amnesty for his
                    supporters and himself, and that the Portuguese commanding officer submitted to
                    the President in his behalf at 10 o’clock last night the terms under which he
                    offers to capitulate, and that the reply is expected to be returned on this
                    day.</p>
            </div>
